{"info":{"author":null,"author_email":"Sarah Hoffmann <lonvia@denofr.de>","bugtrack_url":null,"classifiers":["Development Status :: 5 - Production/Stable","Intended Audience :: Developers","License :: OSI Approved :: BSD License","Programming Language :: C++","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.10","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.11","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.12","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.13","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.14","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.8","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.9","Programming Language :: Python :: Free Threading :: 2 - Beta","Programming Language :: Python :: Implementation :: CPython","Topic :: Scientific/Engineering :: GIS","Typing :: Typed"],"description":"========\npyosmium\n========\n\nThis library provides Python bindings for the `Libosmium`_ C++\nlibrary, a library for working with OpenStreetMap data in a fast and flexible\nmanner.\n\n.. _Libosmium: https://github.com/osmcode/libosmium\n\nInstallation\n============\n\npyosmium can be installed with pip:\n\n    pip install osmium\n\nThe Pypi source package already comes bundled with a matching version of\nlibosmium, protozero and pybind11. Pyosmium additionally depends on\nexpat, libz and libbz2. You need to install\ndevelopment packages for these libraries. On Debian/Ubuntu do::\n\n    sudo apt-get install build-essential cmake libexpat1-dev zlib1g-dev libbz2-dev\n\n\nPython >= 3.8 is supported. Pypy is known not to work.\n\nDocumentation\n=============\n\nThe documentation for the latest release is available at\n`osmcode.org`_.\n\nIf you find bugs or have feature requests, please report those in the\n`Github issue tracker`_. For general questions about using pyosmium you\ncan contanct the `OSM forum`_.\n\n.. _osmcode.org: http://docs.osmcode.org/pyosmium/latest\n.. _Github issue tracker: https://github.com/osmcode/pyosmium/issues/\n.. _OSM forum: https://community.openstreetmap.org/\n\nExamples\n========\n\nThe package contains an `example` directory with small examples on how to use\nthe library. They are mostly ports of the examples in Libosmium and\nosmium-contrib.\n\nAlso check out the `Cookbook section`_ in the documentation.\n\n.. _Cookbook section: https://docs.osmcode.org/pyosmium/latest/cookbooks/\n\nFineprint\n=========\n\nPyosmium is available under the BSD 2-Clause License. See LICENSE.TXT.\n\nThe source code can be found on `GitHub`_.\n\n.. _GitHub: https://github.com/osmcode/pyosmium\n","description_content_type":"text/x-rst","docs_url":null,"download_url":null,"downloads":{"last_day":-1,"last_month":-1,"last_week":-1},"dynamic":null,"home_page":null,"keywords":"OSM, OpenStreetMap, Osmium","license":"BSD-2-Clause","license_expression":null,"license_files":null,"maintainer":null,"maintainer_email":"Sarah Hoffmann <lonvia@denofr.de>","name":"osmium","package_url":"https://pypi.org/project/osmium/","platform":null,"project_url":"https://pypi.org/project/osmium/","project_urls":{"Documentation":"https://docs.osmcode.org/pyosmium/latest/","Homepage":"https://osmcode.org/pyosmium","Issues":"https://github.com/osmcode/pyosmium/issues","Repository":"https://github.com/osmcode/pyosmium"},"provides_extra":["tests","docs"],"release_url":"https://pypi.org/project/osmium/4.3.2/","requires_dist":["requests","pytest; extra == \"tests\"","pytest-httpserver; extra == \"tests\"","pytest-run-parallel; extra == \"tests\"","werkzeug; extra == \"tests\"","shapely; extra == \"tests\"","mkdocs; extra == \"docs\"","mkdocs-material; extra == \"docs\"","mkdocstrings; extra == \"docs\"","mkdocstrings-python; extra == \"docs\"","mkdocs-autorefs; extra == \"docs\"","mkdocs-gen-files; extra == \"docs\"","mkdocs-jupyter; extra == \"docs\"","argparse-manpage; extra == \"docs\""],"requires_python":">=3.8","summary":"Python bindings for libosmium, the data processing library for OSM data","version":"4.3.2","yanked":false,"yanked_reason":null},"last_serial":42409208,"ownership":{"organization":null,"roles":[{"role":"Owner","user":"lonvia"},{"role":"Owner","user":"mtmail"}]},"urls":[{"comment_text":null,"core-metadata":{"sha256":"8e3edcbb2b699eb81b485767977cc6fbc6206746ef93124b8ef04067f2ce0402"},"digests":{"blake2b_256":"9eded0e21305431d0e317fcd68b11416dfbcd67087d5f3d8ba6155199a25e67e","md5":"5b874d5908c79063d872fb74fc1f8ef9","sha256":"63e77e8e49588bea6e37d876686d317e9c97d889bffe20b7ebd5ed721e368964"},"downloads":-1,"filename":"osmium-4.3.2-cp310-cp310-macosx_11_0_arm64.whl","has_sig":false,"md5_digest":"5b874d5908c79063d872fb74fc1f8ef9","packagetype":"bdist_wheel","python_version":"cp310","requires_python":">=3.8","size":1303858,"upload_time":"2026-10-18T19:21:46","upload_time_iso_8601":"2026-10-18T19:21:46.497430Z","url":"https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/9e/de/d0e21305431d0e317fcd68b11416dfbcd67087d5f3d8ba6155199a25e67e/osmium-4.3.2-cp310-cp310-macosx_11_0_arm64.whl","yanked":false,"yanked_reason":null},{"comment_text":null,"core-metadata":{"sha256":"8e3edcbb2b699eb81b485767977cc6fbc6206746ef93124b8ef04067f2ce0402"},"digests":{"blake2b_256":"70aa0cfcd84e9068e9a3af39590dd1104613c440256885401f181e187b8c8a01","md5":"0df5e99ae3e97980d4d37c57bd073a82","sha256":"04754ae2c7e6dce7fe3848fa97d9ff8136be24c0b1fb934eb82b2201f47a9c83"},"downloads":-1,"filename":"osmium-4.3.2-cp310-cp310-macosx_11_0_x86_64.whl","has_sig":false,"md5_digest":"0df5e99ae3e97980d4d37c57bd073a82","packagetype":"bdist_wheel","python_version":"cp310","requires_python":">=3.8","size":1455510,"upload_time":"2026-10-18T19:21:50","upload_time_iso_8601":"2026-10-18T19:21:50.155266Z","url":"https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/70/aa/0cfcd84e9068e9a3af39590dd1104613c440256885401f181e187b8c8a01/osmium-4.3.2-cp310-cp310-macosx_11_0_x86_64.whl","yanked":false,"yanked_reason":null},{"comment_text":null,"core-metadata":{"sha256":"8e3edcbb2b699eb81b485767977cc6fbc6206746ef93124b8ef04067f2ce0402"},"digests":{"blake2b_256":"783c28ce522d1e1529fcd56391e852983cf446032176130f1e818904230838cf","md5":"90ca9d64cae922f6d9cb33e